; Two spellings of a transaction header that beancount documents.
;
; A trailing comment. It is allowed on every other line of a beancount file
; and read off before anything else is asked — a posting, a metadata line, a
; line of its own between entries — and the header is where a person is most
; likely to write one, because that is where they say which statement the
; entry came off. Reading the header to the end of the line without taking the
; comment off first refused the entry, and the message quoted a line that is
; not wrong.
;
; `txn` in place of the flag. Beancount's own documentation gives
; `2014-05-05 txn "Cafe Mogador" "Lamb tagine"` as the alternative to `*`.
; Matched on the flag alone, such an entry matched nothing and was skipped in
; silence with its metadata and its postings — and because its accounts never
; reached the file's used-account set, nothing downstream noticed either: the
; entry was gone and the run reported success with a smaller count.
;
; What this fixture produces: two transactions, both complete.
;
; Verified by tests/integration/test_beancount_reads_what_a_person_writes.py.
2024-01-01 commodity CAD
    gnucash-mnemonic: "CAD"
    gnucash-namespace: "CURRENCY"
    gnucash-fullname: "Canadian Dollar"
    gnucash-fraction: "100"
2024-01-01 open Assets CAD
    gnucash-name: "Assets"
    gnucash-guid: "1111111111111111111111111111111a"
    gnucash-type: "Asset"
    gnucash-placeholder: "False"
2024-01-01 open Assets:Bank CAD
    gnucash-name: "Assets:Bank"
    gnucash-guid: "1111111111111111111111111111111b"
    gnucash-type: "Bank"
    gnucash-placeholder: "False"
2024-01-01 open Expenses CAD
    gnucash-name: "Expenses"
    gnucash-guid: "1111111111111111111111111111111c"
    gnucash-type: "Expense"
    gnucash-placeholder: "False"

2024-02-01 * "Grocer" "Lunch"  ; from the March statement
    gnucash-guid: "2222222222222222222222222222222a"
  Expenses 50.00 CAD
  Assets:Bank -50.00 CAD

2024-02-02 txn "Cafe" "Coffee"
    gnucash-guid: "2222222222222222222222222222222b"
  Expenses 4.25 CAD
  Assets:Bank -4.25 CAD
